<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<%#
  The portal's sitemap (docs/product-refinement/03-documentation-seo.md).

  THREE KINDS OF PAGE, and only one of them was listed. A sitemap that names the articles and not the sections
  they are reached through tells a crawler the sections matter less than the pages inside them, and the portal
  home -- the address every article's own breadcrumb names as its first crumb
  (DocumentationHelper#portal_home_url) -- was not listed at all.

  The articles' and the categories' alternates come from the same helper the pages' own
  `<link rel="alternate">` tags come from (`documentation_layout/articles/_meta_head.html.erb:19-24`,
  `documentation_layout/categories/_meta_head.html.erb`), so the sitemap and the page cannot disagree. THE
  PORTAL HOME CARRIES NO ALTERNATES HERE because it carries no head tags at all: `rel="canonical"` appears in
  exactly two templates in `app/views` and `portals/show.html+documentation.erb` is neither of them, so the
  home has no canonical and no hreflang of its own. Inventing a set here that the page does not publish is
  exactly the disagreement this file exists to avoid. The missing head is submitted as a requested change
  rather than worked around.

  Each locale's article has its own slug and its own canonical, so each is its own <url>, and the xhtml:link
  alternates inside the entry are what tell a crawler the entries are one page in two languages.

  Published only, and alternates are published only too: announcing a draft translation earns a soft-404.
  `lastmod` is the article's own updated_at, which is the only modification date this product actually records.
  A category and the portal home have no modification date of their own -- inventing one from the newest
  article inside them would be a number nobody stated -- so those entries carry no `lastmod` rather than a
  guess. `lastmod` is optional in the protocol; a wrong one is worse than none.

  NO <image:image> ENTRIES, and this is a decision rather than an omission (R2-MEDIA-CONTRACT.md).
  Three measured reasons. The corpus contains no image reference at all today -- a no-exclusion
  `grep -rn '!\[' custom/db/documentation custom/db/changelog` over 128 Markdown files returns one hit, and it
  is the example in the comment at `custom/db/documentation/media/.keep:3`, not an article -- so the markup
  would be dead on arrival. Resolving the keys would mean one `Documentation::MediaResolver` per article, and a
  resolver instance loads the PORTAL's whole media set to build its index (R2-MEDIA-INTERFACE.md §2.4), so an
  N-article sitemap would do N full media loads to emit tags for screenshots of a dashboard. And the images
  are UI screenshots: the image-search traffic an image sitemap exists to win is not traffic this corpus has.
  If that changes, the entry point is this file plus one resolver built once outside the loop -- recorded here
  so the next reader does not have to rediscover the shape.
%>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
  <%#
    The portal home, once per locale the portal actually allows. `allowed_locale_codes` rather than the
    distinct locales of the rows, because a locale removed from the portal's configuration is no longer
    served and must not be announced.
  %>
  <% @portal.allowed_locale_codes.each do |locale| %>
    <url>
      <loc><%= portal_home_url(@portal, locale) %></loc>
    </url>
  <% end %>

  <% @portal.categories.sort_by { |category| [category.locale, category.slug] }.each do |category| %>
    <% next unless @portal.allowed_locale_codes.include?(category.locale) %>
    <url>
      <loc><%= portal_category_canonical_url(@portal, category) %></loc>
      <% portal_category_locale_alternates(@portal, category).each do |locale, url| %>
        <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="<%= html_lang_attribute(locale) %>" href="<%= url %>"/>
      <% end %>
      <% if (default_url = portal_category_default_alternate_url(@portal, category)) %>
        <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="<%= default_url %>"/>
      <% end %>
    </url>
  <% end %>

  <% @portal.articles.where(status: :published).includes(:root_article).each do |article| %>
    <url>
      <loc><%= portal_canonical_url(@portal, article) %></loc>
      <lastmod><%= article.updated_at.to_date.iso8601 %></lastmod>
      <% portal_locale_alternates(@portal, article).each do |locale, url| %>
        <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="<%= html_lang_attribute(locale) %>" href="<%= url %>"/>
      <% end %>
      <% if (default_url = portal_default_alternate_url(@portal, article)) %>
        <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="<%= default_url %>"/>
      <% end %>
    </url>
  <% end %>
</urlset>
